      "ScopeManifest": {
        "description": "Everything an assessment needs to run narrowed, and a hash that identifies it.\n\nDETERMINISTIC, WHICH IS WHY THIS SERVICE HOLDS NO STATE. `scope_id` is a hash over the\nbank version and the normalised request, so `GET /scopes/{id}` recomputes rather than\nlooks up. The service scales horizontally for free and a restart loses nothing \u2014 the\nsame property, for the same reason, as `competency-graph`.\n\n`bank_version` is carried so a session can refuse a scope built against a bank that has\nsince been replaced. Without it the orchestrator would happily apply an allowlist naming\nitems that no longer exist, and the symptom would be a competency that exhausts\nimmediately for no stated reason.",
        "properties": {
          "bank_id": {
            "title": "Bank Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "bank_version": {
            "title": "Bank Version",
            "type": "string"
          },
